WEBVTT

1
00:12:04.000 --> 00:12:13.000
Nathan B.: Our $49 floor blocks single-practitioner clinics. I'd add a $19 entry tier with a 60-day trial.

2
00:12:40.000 --> 00:12:49.000
Smith: Competitors anchor at $25 to $29, so $19 reads as an entry offer, not a discount.

3
00:14:32.000 --> 00:14:37.000
Emma C.: Then we need to rewrite pricing for self-serve by Friday.

4
00:16:38.000 --> 00:16:40.000
Nathan B.: The creative already assumes $19. We can't move it.

5
00:16:40.000 --> 00:16:44.000
Emma C.: Agreed. We ship the $19 tier before the Q4 campaign.

6
00:18:05.000 --> 00:18:10.000
Emma C.: Wait, this is basically the pricing ticket we already have.

7
00:22:15.000 --> 00:22:27.000
Nathan B.: Existing annual plans are the open risk; no customer should pay more after the change. If the pricing copy freezes Friday, engineering can cut the release on Monday.

8
00:22:28.000 --> 00:22:31.000
Emma C.: Copy freezes Friday. Deal.

9
00:22:40.000 --> 00:22:46.000
Nathan B.: I'll keep an eye on the annual-plan migration until the release branch is cut.

10
00:28:10.000 --> 00:28:18.000
Smith: Clinics compare per-practitioner price, not per-site. I'd lead the page with that unit.

11
00:33:50.000 --> 00:33:56.000
Emma C.: Does the 60-day trial apply to clinics that churned in the last year?

12
00:41:10.000 --> 00:41:16.000
Nathan B.: Okay, let's get legal to look at the annual wording before it goes live.
